	},
	"connections": [
		{
			"to": "western-civ/rite-of-spring",
			"why": "The Skandalkonzert of Schoenberg's circle in Vienna on 31 March 1913, which this frame tells, ended in a brawl two months before the Paris premiere of The Rite of Spring, and that frame names it among the year's upheavals."
		},
		{
			"to": "mathematics/groups",
			"why": "A twelve-tone row's four forms, prime, retrograde, inversion and retrograde inversion, combine by the rules of a group as that frame defines one, with a Cayley table of their own: the Klein four-group, named in 1884 by Felix Klein, whom that frame introduces."
		},
		{
			"to": "western-civ/holocaust",
			"why": "The Nazi civil-service law of 7 April 1933 that opens that frame's steps is the law under which the Prussian Academy of Arts dismissed Schoenberg, who went into exile in the United States."
		}
	],
